WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.237
-Our next guest was an NFL
quarterback for 17 seasons

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:06.506
and is now an analyst
for Prime Video's

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.141
"Thursday Night Football,"
which premieres

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.876
next Thursday, September 15th.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:13.379
Please welcome to the show
Ryan Fitzpatrick, everyone.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.281
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:20.987 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:26.693 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.027
-Alright.
-Thank you for being here.

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:32.164
-Thank you for having me.
-So, 17 seasons in the league.

00:00:32.164 --> 00:00:34.500
And I'm just wondering
over the course of that time,

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.802
did you ever
picture broadcasting

00:00:36.802 --> 00:00:38.604
being the next step?
Did you consider coaching?

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.573
Or did you just think
you were going to play forever?

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:43.009
Because very few people
do 17 years.

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:45.612
-I thought I could play forever.
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.213
-Had a hip injury last year,

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.449
so age started catching up
with me a little bit,

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:52.718
but I think those are
the two natural avenues --

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:53.953
coaching and broadcasting.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:55.354
Just because it's something

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:59.058
I've essentially dedicated
my whole life to doing.

00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:02.462
But coaching is very hard.
A lot of hours.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.930
My kids would be, you know,
not real happy with Dad,

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:08.668
so the broadcasting thing
I think is going to be fun.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.970
I think I've got a lot of
experiences I can share.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.239
And Amazon, with Prime Video

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.107
and this new "Thursday Night
Football" package

00:01:15.107 --> 00:01:16.542
seemed like
the right fit for me.

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:17.944
-That's also a very important
thing to note.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:20.045
You actually had
a broadcasting job,

00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:22.315
a football broadcasting job,
and you don't work weekends,

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.116
which is, for your children,
very kind.

00:01:24.116 --> 00:01:25.384
-Which is huge.
-Yeah.

00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:27.253
-So I can still be soccer dad.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:28.721
I can still watch
all of the stuff

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.356
that goes on
Friday, Saturday, Sunday.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:31.824
It's going to be great.

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:36.829
-And we should know that
you're not just a one-kid dad.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.964
-We've got seven.
We've got seven little ones.

00:01:38.964 --> 00:01:41.301
-You've got seven kids.
-Yeah, which you have three?

00:01:41.301 --> 00:01:43.069
-I have three,
and I'm walking around

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:46.072
being like,
"I'm a real big shot," but, no.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:49.209
-I will tell you,
I also feel like I'm a big shot,

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:53.179
but my wife left out of town
for about a week.

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:55.848
-Wow!
-So I had all seven of them.

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:57.817
-And is it 3 to 15?
Is that the ages?

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:01.821
-3 to 15.
All the odd years in between.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.589
And I just had to
get out of the way.

00:02:03.589 --> 00:02:05.558
They are well-trained.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.927
They asked me to pour milk,
like, in the cereal bowl.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.829
That was, like, Dad's role
for the week basically.

00:02:10.829 --> 00:02:12.332
And then one of
my four daughters

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.800
asked me to braid her hair.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.070
So I've got the double braid
where you start the braid,

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.738
and the hair gets all weird,

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:22.108
so you put the tie in
and then you braid more.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.176
I call it the double braid,
and it's what they love.

00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:26.011
-Okay. Great.
What is the --

00:02:26.011 --> 00:02:29.482
Just for the logistics
of seven children,

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:32.151
what is the transportation
situation?

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:34.553
-So, it's the only time
we ever had to think about,

00:02:34.553 --> 00:02:36.355
are we having another kid?

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:38.024
Because when you go
from six to seven,

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.559
you go from minivan
to something else.

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:42.562
So we no longer fit
in a minivan.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:46.666
We got a big old
12-passenger van,

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.734
which is great
when all the kids are in it.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:51.103
And then when I'm driving it
by myself,

00:02:51.103 --> 00:02:54.173
people are like, "Eh.
I don't know about that guy."

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:55.608
-Yeah, I will say, like,

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:58.111
that beard
and an empty passenger van?

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.812
-[ Laughs ] It's not great.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.347
-It's not great.
-Not great.

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.616
I often have lots of candy, too.
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:06.319
Well, of course, seven kids.
You're gonna have candy, yeah.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.754
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:11.724
Do you -- You played for --
How many different teams

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:14.126
did you play for
over your 17 years?

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:15.528
-Nine.
-Nine.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.430
And does that mean
that you have fan bases

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.865
everywhere that consider you
one of theirs?

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:23.135
Are you often approached?
-Yeah, I do.

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:26.372
I would say Buffalo,

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:29.875
the Jets, Miami --

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:31.543
those are probably the three --

00:03:31.543 --> 00:03:33.546
Tampa. Those are the four that
if I'm getting approached

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:36.482
in an airport, like,
it's probably one of those four.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.684
It's probably
not St. Louis Rams

00:03:38.684 --> 00:03:41.086
and Tennessee and Cincinnati
and those teams.

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:43.656
But, yeah, it's always
interesting, like,

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:45.391
"Okay, what are they
going to come up

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.893
and say to me
when they approach me?"

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:50.696
-How about New York?
How do you get treated here?

00:03:50.696 --> 00:03:53.032
-You know, 2015 season,
if they remember you

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:55.501
from that season,
they loved me, most of it.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.936
2016, not so much.

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:59.705
So it's like
a 50/50 proposition.

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:01.174
-This is from today.
You got recognized.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.342
-This is from today.
We were having a slice of pizza.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:05.711
[ Laughter ]
-And this is --

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:07.513
I mean, that shows --

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.815
When you got
a demographic of fan

00:04:09.815 --> 00:04:11.551
who's not using a phone.

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:14.787
-Yeah.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:17.056
So I think he may --

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:21.027
We were talking about streaming
football on Thursday nights.

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:23.262
I don't know that
he's going to be set up

00:04:23.262 --> 00:04:24.931
for the first week to do it.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.766
But we're going to get him
his Prime membership.

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.067
-You mentioned Buffalo.

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:31.704
Buffalo had an incredible
first week of playoff football

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.205
last year
against the Patriots,

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:34.774
which is obviously a team,
you know --

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.475
Everybody in the AFC East
has had trouble

00:04:36.475 --> 00:04:37.943
with the Patriots
over the years.

00:04:37.943 --> 00:04:40.446
Huge win. You went to the game.

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:41.547
First of all, very impressed.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.715
You did not do
the luxury-box path.

00:04:43.715 --> 00:04:45.184
You went and sat with the fans.

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:46.785
How many of your kids
did you bring with you?

00:04:46.785 --> 00:04:48.021
-My two oldest.

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:50.656
At the time,
my boys were 14 and 12.

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:53.258
-And it was negative-10 degrees.
-Yeah.

00:04:53.258 --> 00:04:55.194
-Here's the photo of you
and I think your oldest.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:58.697
Now, how did it come about

00:04:58.697 --> 00:05:00.966
that you guys decided
to go shirtless?

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:04.236
-The whole way walking through
the parking lot into the gates,

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:05.972
well, they learned
some new words.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:07.539
We had a guy
with a Mac Jones Jersey

00:05:07.539 --> 00:05:11.177
walking by us, and so plenty
of expletives being thrown.

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:12.878
But my boys the whole time
were like,

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:15.214
"Dad. Shirts off. Shirts off."

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:18.083
So it was just -- I felt like
I was in college again,

00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:19.952
getting peer-pressured
to, like, go drinking

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.687
or something, you know?

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:24.957
And so the Bills score
seven touchdowns in a row,

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.893
which, like, has never happened.

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:29.662
And I thought,
"This is the moment, boys."

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:31.564
And so we ripped them off and --

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:33.465
-I would imagine
the fans in the area

00:05:33.465 --> 00:05:36.502
were pretty proud of you
as a former Bill.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.537
-Well, and we had --
Then other people started

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:40.106
taking their shirts off,
as well.

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:42.675
-So the peer pressure
goes both ways.

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:45.378
-Yeah, it does, it does.
-This is one of my favorites.

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:47.813
I remember this photo
from a press conference.

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:51.650
DeSean Jackson was a
wide receiver with you in Tampa.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:55.554
And can you explain how
you ended up in his clothes?

00:05:55.554 --> 00:05:58.824
-So D-Jack walks through
the locker room,

00:05:58.824 --> 00:06:00.993
and what he's wearing,
I just --

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:03.296
I felt like it was something
I could never get away with.

00:06:03.296 --> 00:06:05.064
Anything he wears looks cool.
-Yeah.

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:06.732
-And I'm always
complimenting him.

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:10.035
And so he walks through
with this get-up and chains.

00:06:10.035 --> 00:06:11.704
I'm like, "D-Jack,
I could never wear that.

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:14.206
People would just laugh me
off the stage, essentially."

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:16.642
And he said, "Well, if we
win today, you're wearing it."

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:20.513
And so, we win the game, press
conference comes up, and...

00:06:20.513 --> 00:06:22.348
-And I got to be honest.
You pull it off.

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:24.183
-It's not bad, right?
-It's not bad.

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:25.985
-But he's --
It's really not bad.

00:06:25.985 --> 00:06:27.887
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.789
-Yeah.

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:33.058
-He's 60 pounds lighter than me,
so it was a little snug.

00:06:33.058 --> 00:06:34.527
-Yeah, it's a little snug,

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:36.528
but this is really
the highest compliment.

00:06:36.528 --> 00:06:38.063
I mean, I can tell you
you pulled it off,

00:06:38.063 --> 00:06:41.033
but then your son decided
to wear it for Halloween.

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:44.036
-Yes.
-So he really pulls it off.

00:06:44.036 --> 00:06:46.305
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:48.240
-With the pencilled-in
chest hair there, too.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.409
With the pencilled-in
chest hair.

00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:53.479
For me, that's the highest
compliment as a father --

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:56.682
your son dressing up like you
for Halloween.

00:06:56.682 --> 00:07:00.820
I felt like nowhere to go
but down now as a father.

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:04.123
-Also, it should be noted
Richard Sherman, Al Michaels --

00:07:04.123 --> 00:07:07.493
You're really with one of the
all-time greats in the booth.

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:09.461
-So, Al Michaels
and Kirk Herbstreit,

00:07:09.461 --> 00:07:12.231
which they're both --
The voices are iconic.

00:07:12.231 --> 00:07:14.566
When Al's just telling
a conversation

00:07:14.566 --> 00:07:17.403
and he's speaking,
he's ordering a steak for lunch,

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:20.205
you're just mesmerized
by his voice.

00:07:20.205 --> 00:07:22.141
Yeah, and then Richard Sherman
is going to be great.

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:23.875
He's freshly off the field,
as well.

00:07:23.875 --> 00:07:26.379
And he's a defensive guy,
so I think we're going to have

00:07:26.379 --> 00:07:28.781
a lot of battles in terms
of what we like going on

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.216
in the game and what we don't.

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:31.650
That's going to be
real interesting.

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.686
And then the hall-of-famer
Tony Gonzalez

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:36.188
and Charissa Thompson.
-Well, it's a great group.

00:07:36.188 --> 00:07:37.857
And it was really exciting
and cool

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:39.658
to watch you for 17 years
on the field,

00:07:39.658 --> 00:07:42.060
and I'm really excited for
this next chapter, as well.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:43.763
Thanks for making time
for us, man.

00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:45.497
Ryan Fitzpatrick, everybody.

00:07:45.497 --> 00:07:46.865
"Thursday Night Football"

00:07:46.865 --> 00:07:49.068
premieres Thursday,
September 15th, on Prime Video.

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:51.237
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

